bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    text_len_codepoint_switch_2026-11-03, 0, "2026-11-10 fix lane (Fable). Seed-side switch is already in source on release/1.0.0: interpreter len/slice/substring/index_of count code points via interpreter_method/mod.rs text_cp_len (PR7877 04969955c75) and the native/JIT lane routes text .len() to rt_string_char_count (row text_len_bytes_vs_codepoint_index_bound_disagree_2026_11_03). The deployed Windows seed C:/dev/simple/bin/simple.exe (2026-11-04) predates the flip and still prints len=9 for \"héllo€\". Added pinning tests: Rust text_cp_len_counts_code_points_not_bytes + interpreter_text_len_is_code_points_and_byte_len_is_bytes (interpreter_method/mod.rs tests, green via cargo test --lib -p simple-compiler) and spec test/01_unit/lib/text/text_len_codepoint_spec.spl (ASCII, 2/3/4-byte, combining sequence, byte_len stays bytes): RED on the 2026-11-04 seed (1 passed / 5 failed), green expected on a seed rebuilt from this source. Still OPEN for follow-up (not this lane): migration of the ~535 byte-offset .len() callers in src/compiler + src/lib to byte_len(), and Phase 3 stage2/stage3 self-hosted parity."
